    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green. Here's a summary of what I did.\n\n## What changed\n\nI unified `customerCode` + `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` (e.g. the test run produced `NSW2716E6609E1` = `NSW` + FY `27` + HASH8 `16E6609E` + Luhn CHK `1`), and removed the derived `checkDigit` field.\n\n**Identity assignment**\n- Added `rest/function/owner/AssignMemberId.java` \u2014 computes region (`LocalityResolver`), the 2-digit fiscal year (`FiscalYear` over the business-day-adjusted registration date), HASH8 (`Sha256Hash.upperHex(telephone + lastName, 8)`, the same hash the region-and-hash identity used), and CHK (`CheckDigit.luhnOf(<REGION><FY><HASH8>)`). Collision handling now de-duplicates the **memberId** by appending `-<n>`.\n- Deleted `AssignCustomerCode.java` and `AssignMembershipNumber.java`.\n- `owners.POST.yml`: replaced the two `assignCustomerCode`/`assignMembershipNumber` steps with a single `assignMemberId` step.\n\n**Model & schema**\n- `Owner.java`: replaced `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` fields/accessors with `memberId` (`member_id` column).\n- `db/h2/schema.sql` and `db/hsqldb/schema.sql`: `customer_code` + `membership_number` \u2192 `member_id VARCHAR(30)`.\n\n**DTO & mapping**\n- `openapi.yml`: removed `customerCode`, `checkDigit`, `membershipNumber`; added `memberId` (regenerates `OwnerDto.get/setMemberId`).\n- `OwnerMapper.java`: removed the `checkDigit` mapping and its `CheckDigit` import; `memberId` maps by name; `locality`/`timezone`/`ownerSegment` now derive region from the memberId.\n- `LocalityResolver.regionOfCustomerCode` \u2192 `regionOfMemberId`, parsing the region as the leading letter run (terminated by the FY digits) \u2014 so the **owner segment** references the memberId.\n\n**Audit**\n- `AuditOwnerCreated.java`: log line now carries `memberId` (dropped `customerCode`/`membershipNumber`).\n- `OwnerCreatedEvent.java`: primary identifier is now `owner.getMemberId()` and the JSON key is `memberId`.\n\n**Docs**: updated javadocs in `CheckDigit`, `Sha256Hash`, and `BusinessDay` to reference the memberId.\n\n**Tests:** `mvnw test` \u2192 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`. The acceptance test confirms `memberId` starts with `NSW`, contains the SHA-256 HASH8, and that `customerCode`/`membershipNumber` are absent.",
